INTERPRETATION
- BC_only tests the S581/S595 large-owner automaton after Bprime and Lemma C.
- full_stack first removes S598 total/one-sided caps and Lemmas E/F.
- singleton_empty is often a local one-component determinant wall; pair_empty
  is the first genuinely Helly-style two-row obstruction.
- bounded_live rows are not counterexamples; they are places where this
  bounded-window certificate did not yet kill the S' family.

TOURNAMENT ANALYSIS
vertices: determinant certificate sizes, not runners or raw arcs
pair observable: (certificate_rank, sampled_route_count, name)
switch/gauge: smaller empty determinant subfamily beats larger/global residue burden
score_hist={0: 1, 1: 1, 2: 1, 3: 1, 4: 1, 5: 1, 6: 1}; directed_3_cycles=0; SCCs=(1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1); Hamiltonian_paths=1; tie_HP=singleton_empty > pair_empty > triple_empty > quad_empty > high_order_empty > bounded_live > preempted_gate

ASSUMPTION CHALLENGE
Alternative vertices considered: runners, gaps, cap centers, components,
endpoint owners, owner pairs, residue classes, prime powers, and proof obligations.
Chosen vertices are determinant component languages and minimal empty subsets.
The quotient preserves bounded cover feasibility for v=nw before dominance;
it destroys phase order beyond the bounded w window and the full CRT modulus.
Challenged assumption: automaton emptiness need not be proved globally first;
a small Helly witness may be the human proof object.
